{"records":[{"id":"7pphhgrwfn","title":"Understanding and Avoiding Plagiarism","description":"Plagiarism remains a challenge for most academic and professional institutions. The paper identifies the forms, consequences and provide practical ways to avoid plagiarism.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-20T18:49:46.539Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7pphhgrwfn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7pphhgrwfn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Library","last_name":"BTUC","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Education","Academic Writing","Information"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"n4n4r74bgz","title":"Spectroscopic data of pleural effusion","description":"Pleural effusion is a medical condition having its etiology in various primary diseases, eg. cardiological, pulmonological, and oncological. It is a side effect of diseases such as pneumonia, tuberculosis, cancer, heart failure, and inflammation which are responsible for causing inflammatory diseases of the pleura. Late detection of pleural effusion disturbs the respiratory function, heart operation or may cause bleeding into the pleural cavity. In such a case, there is an immediate requirement for medical intervention and drainage of the pleural space or execution of pleurodesis causing pleural plaques to fuse, which is an invasive and potentially life-threatening procedure.\nTherefore, patients with fluid in the pleural cavity, especially a group with recurrent pleural effusion should be continuously monitored.\nIn a standard clinical procedure, the presence of pleural effusion is diagnosed by a physician with the use of chest radiography, ultrasonography, or computed tomography. Although ultrasound becomes portable and handheld the diagnosis is possible only in the clinics or medical centers so far. The monitoring of pleural effusion in outpatients is still an unsolved problem.\nSo far, the use of near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) to test the amount of hydro-derivative fluids in various biomedical applications has been developed. For example, a method for assessing brain edema, water composition in rabbit meal, the water content in moisturizing creams or ceramic plasters has been published. In this work, the data form noninvasive NIRS measurement in patients with pleural effusion were collected. The method for noninvasive detection of pleural effusion using continuous-wave near-infrared spectroscopy is presented. The method has been developed based on numerical simulations of light transport in turbid media and validated on phantoms mimicking tissues and on patients with excess pleural fluid undergoing thoracocentesis. \nNumerical simulations consisted in modeling light propagation in an optically turbid, non-homogeneous medium with tissue properties of peripulmonary structures and for various amounts of pleural fluid. A three-layer model depicting pleural effusion was adopted. It was assumed that the outer surface layer consists of skin, fat and muscle. Fiber optics were connected to this layer during measurements. Two fiber optics were used: one guiding the light from the source (emitter) and the second delivering to the spectrometer (detector). The second layer, present only when pleural effusion is present, is water layer. The third layer is the lung tissue layer. The NIRS measurement was performed in a reflective scenario. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-11-23T06:57:47.846Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/n4n4r74bgz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/n4n4r74bgz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"SensoriumLab","last_name":"Library","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/05pwfyy15","name":"National Centre for Research and Development","grant_id":"POIR.01.01.01-00-0824/17"}],"categories":["Spectroscopy"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ynv4mn4k4m","title":"A method for rapid nanobody screening with no bias of the library diversity","description":"We dedeveloped a methodfor rapid nanobody screening with no bias of the library diversity. The Dataset herein make the primary data available. The files are supplementary raw data used to make all the graphs in the manuscript and uncropped images for all the blots in the manuscript.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-13T13:19:38.13Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ynv4mn4k4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ynv4mn4k4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhiqing","last_name":"Tao","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiaoling","last_name":"Zhao","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Huan","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lichun","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/027s68j25","name":"Ministry of Science and Technology of the People's Republic of China","grant_id":"2018YFE0202301 "},{"id":null,"name":"National Natural Sciences Foundation of China grants","grant_id":"22174151"},{"id":null,"name":"Hubei Provincial Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":"2023AFA041"},{"id":"https://ror.org/027s68j25","name":"Ministry of Science and Technology of the People's Republic of China","grant_id":"2018YFE0202300"},{"id":null,"name":" the Strategic Priority Research Program of the Chinese Academy of Sciences ","grant_id":"XDB0540000"},{"id":null,"name":"Natural Science Foundation of Shandong grants","grant_id":"ZR2022MH282"},{"id":null,"name":"National Natural Sciences Foundation of China grants","grant_id":"21991080"}],"categories":["Data Quality","Primary Data"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3n5hzxt58t","title":"Brunello Whole Genome Knockout library in BE(2)-C Neuroblastoma cells, LACV Survival Selected","description":"NGS data of library population subjected to LACV survival selection. \nHuman Brunello CRISPR knockout pooled library was a gift from David Root and John Doench (Addgene #73178). \nBE(2)-C cells from ATCC CRL-2268.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-26T08:50:27.879Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3n5hzxt58t","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3n5hzxt58t"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lisa","last_name":"Francomacaro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroblastoma","Genomic Library","La Crosse Virus","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Knock Out","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8cj9tzb4pz","title":"Brunello Whole Genome Knockout library in BE(2)-C Neuroblastoma cells, INKV Survival Selected","description":"NGS data of library population subjected to INKV survival selection. \nHuman Brunello CRISPR knockout pooled library was a gift from David Root and John Doench (Addgene #73178). \nBE(2)-C cells from ATCC CRL-2268.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-26T08:57:31.02Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8cj9tzb4pz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8cj9tzb4pz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lisa","last_name":"Francomacaro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroblastoma","Orthobunyavirus","Genomic Library","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Knock Out","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"57zhhhs7xz","title":"Metagenomic Dataset  of an Eastern spinebill (Acanthorhynchus tenuirostris) ","description":"2.1 Source of sampling and extraction of DNA\nDroppings was collected from a holding bag of an Eastern spinebill caught in a mist net as part of a fauna survey in the Windsor Downs Reserve Nature (33°39’0.42’S, 150°48’31.97”E), New South Wales (Australian Bird and Bat Banding Scheme (ABBBS) Banding Authority Number 1893,  ABBBS project approval - cooperative project 8529, New South Wales National Parks and Wildlife Service - Scientific License No. SL101929). The total genomic DNA was extracted using a commercial kit (PurelinkTM Genomic DNA Mini Kit, Invitrogen, California, USA) according to the manufacturer’s instructions.\n\n\n2.2 Library construction and sequencing\nThe library preparation and sequencing was performed as previously described (Sarker et al., 2020; Sarker et al., 2018; Sarker et al., 2017b). Briefly, the paired-end library with an insert size of 150 bp was prepared using the QIAseq FX DNA Library Kit (Qiagen) starting with ten ng of total genomic DNA (gDNA). The amplified library was cleaned to remove PCR-generated adaptor-dimers using JetSeq™ Clean beads (Bioline) according to the protocol described in QIAseq FX DNA Library Kits. The quality and quantity of the prepared library was assessed using an Agilent Tape Station (Agilent Technologies) by the Genomic Platform, La Trobe University. The prepared library was normalised and pooled in equimolar quantities. Cluster generation and sequencing of the pooled DNA-library was sequenced on Illumina® NextSeq500 platform according to the manufacturer’s instructions (Australian Genome Research Facility, Melbourne).","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-04-06T07:25:05.893Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/57zhhhs7xz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/57zhhhs7xz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Subir","last_name":"Sarker","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Next Generation Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"m8pkzbktbk","title":"Brunello Whole Genome Knock out library in BE(2)-C Neuroblastoma cells - NGS dataset of library population","description":"NGS data to confirm representative and balanced creation of the Brunello whole genome knock out library in BE(2)-C neuroblastoma cells. \nHuman Brunello CRISPR knockout pooled library was a gift from David Root and John Doench (Addgene #73178). \nBE(2)-C cells from ATCC CRL-2268.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-11-01T07:40:29.578Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/m8pkzbktbk","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/m8pkzbktbk"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lisa","last_name":"Francomacaro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroblastoma","Genomic Library","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Knock Out","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zcnyfzjvhw","title":"Computational wave optics library for C++: CWO++ library ","description":"Abstract \n Diffraction calculations, such as the angular spectrum method and Fresnel diffractions, are used for calculating scalar light propagation. The calculations are used in wide-ranging optics fields: for example, Computer Generated Holograms (CGHs), digital holography, diffractive optical elements, microscopy, image encryption and decryption, three-dimensional analysis for optical devices and so on. However, increasing demands made by large-scale diffraction calculations have rendered the computa...\n \n Title of program: CWO++\n Catalogue Id: AELL_v1_0\n \n Nature of problem \n The CWO++ library provides diffraction calculations which are useful for computer generated holograms (CGHs), digital holography, diffractive optical elements, microscopy, image encryption and decryption and three-dimensional analysis for optical devices.\n \n Versions of this program held in the CPC repository in Mendeley Data\n AELL_v1_0; CWO++; 10.1016/j.cpc.2011.12.027\n \n This program has been imported from the CPC Program Library held at Queen's University Belfast (1969-2018)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2012-05-01T11:00:00Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zcnyfzjvhw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zcnyfzjvhw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Tomoyoshi","last_name":"Shimobaba","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiantong","last_name":"Weng","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Takahiro","last_name":"Sakurai","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Naohisa","last_name":"Okada","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Takashi","last_name":"Nishitsuji","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Naoki","last_name":"Takada","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Atsushi","last_name":"Shiraki","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nobuyuki","last_name":"Masuda","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tomoyoshi","last_name":"Ito","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Optics","Computational Physics"],"journal_issn":["00104655"]},{"id":"2kbjft8jd3","title":"Library for : 14-3-3ζ-c-Src-integrin-β3 complex is vital for platelet activation","description":"The library using for virtual screening, after removed unpublished compounds.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-04-21T08:39:42.661Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2kbjft8jd3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2kbjft8jd3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Gan","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Library"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vvtfdgfk76","title":"A broad-spectrum antiviral molecule, protoporphyrin IX, acts as a moderator of HIV-1 capsid assembly by targeting the capsid hexamer","description":"Information of drug library used and The results of drug screening.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-07-25T18:40:10.457Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vvtfdgfk76","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vvtfdgfk76"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Dawei","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Drug Screening"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":58557,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":79,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":58557,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":58466,"restricted":38,"embargoed":53},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":914},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":357},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":276},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":231},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":225},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":213},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":193},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":158},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":130},{"id":"https://ror.org/04q48ey07","name":"National Institute of General Medical Sciences","count":115}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":56294},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1853},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":129},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":63},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":40},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":34},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":26},{"id":"5f1edf21-7948-4d82-894f-c0ed4b1e8f52","name":"Teesside University","count":